@startuml 00-system-context
!include ../_style.iuml
title Nós no Cabo — System context (current state)

actor "Visitor" as visitor
actor "Site owner\n(submitter)" as owner
actor "Admin" as admin

rectangle "nos-client\nReact SPA (Vite)" as spa
rectangle "nos-sr\nFlask API :3000" as api
database "PostgreSQL 15\n(webring)" as db

rectangle "Member websites\n(embed webring badge)" as members <<external>>
rectangle "OpenLibrary API\nopenlibrary.org" as openlib <<external>>
rectangle "Unicorn Studio\n(3D scene, 404 page)" as unicorn <<external>>
rectangle "MSW worker\n(in-browser mock API)" as msw <<mocked>>

visitor --> spa : browse feed,\nwebsite details
owner --> spa : submit site\n(6-step wizard)
admin --> spa : same UI;\nadmin mode if\nVITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD set

spa --> api : REST/JSON (axios)
spa ..> msw : when VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS != 'false'\n(default ON)
spa --> openlib : book recommendations\n(direct from browser)
spa --> unicorn : scene JSON (public/)
api --> db : SQLAlchemy
api --> members : scrape metadata\n(requests + BeautifulSoup)
members --> api : visitors via\nGET /nos/:code redirect

note right of admin
  <b>No real auth.</b> Admin = shared password
  sent as <i>x-admin-password</i>. The client reads
  it from VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD, so it is
  shipped in the JS bundle.
end note

note bottom of msw
  Mocks are ON by default: a build that
  forgets VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS=false talks
  to fake data.
end note

@enduml
